 ### Integer Hash Map with Chaining
-A hash table implementation for integer keys using open addressing via chaining [S6, unofficial]. It supports hashing 2 or 4 integer keys into a single index using bit masking and shifting (e.g., 10 bits per key for 2 keys, 5 bits for 4 keys) [S6, unofficial]. Memory management requires explicit destructor calls to traverse and delete chains [S6, unofficial].
